<p>For maximum protection, consignors should opt for a <strong>100% declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong>. Unlike standard policies that cap coverage at a lower percentage of the bike’s value, a 100% policy ensures that the entire declared value is covered in the event of loss, damage, or theft.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This type of coverage is especially critical for premium or vintage motorcycles, where the replacement cost can far exceed the standard insurance limits.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By declaring the full value and securing a 100% marine transit policy, consignors eliminate the risk of under‑insurance and streamline the claims process, guaranteeing that the bike’s worth is fully protected from the moment it leaves the yard until it arrives at its destination.</span></li></ul>

<p>In summary, meticulous paperwork coupled with comprehensive insurance creates a robust safety net. By ensuring each document is accurate, current, and properly filed, consignors can focus on what matters most: getting their prized bike to its new home without unexpected delays or financial surprises.</p></div>
